PKªS’ïÀ␀␀À␀␀PK
␀␀␀␀cs]␀␀␀␀N␀␀N␀␀n␀ ␀banlan-supplement-2026-11-20/workspace/packages/banlan-miniapp-frontend/node_modules/qrcode-terminal/README.mdUT␀•{˛jcF␀k¢{˛jux␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀# QRCode Terminal Edition [![Build Status][travis-ci-img]][travis-ci-url]

> Going where no QRCode has gone before.

![Basic Example][basic-example-img]

# Node Library

## Install

Can be installed with:

    $ npm install qrcode-terminal

and used:

    var qrcode = require('qrcode-terminal');

## Usage

To display some data to the terminal just call:

    qrcode.generate('This will be a QRCode, eh!');

You can even specify the error level (default is 'L'):
    
    qrcode.setErrorLevel('Q');
    qrcode.generate('This will be a QRCode with error level Q!');

If you don't want to display to the terminal but just want to string you can provide a callback:

    qrcode.generate('http://github.com', function (qrcode) {
        console.log(qrcode);
    });

If you want to display small output, provide `opts` with `small`:

    qrcode.generate('This will be a small QRCode, eh!', {small: true});

    qrcode.generate('This will be a small QRCode, eh!', {small: true}, function (qrcode) {
        console.log(qrcode)
    });

# Command-Line

## Install

    $ npm install -g qrcode-terminal

## Usage

    $ qrcode-terminal --help
    $ qrcode-terminal 'http://github.com'
    $ echo 'http://github.com' | qrcode-terminal

# Support

- OS X
- Linux
- Windows

# Server-side

[node-qrcode][node-qrcode-url] is a popular server-side QRCode generator that
renders to a `canvas` object.

# Developing

To setup the development envrionment run `npm install`

To run tests run `npm test`

# Contributers

    Gord Tanner <gtanner@gmail.com>
    Micheal Brooks <michael@michaelbrooks.ca>

